<title>LEBANON: Lebanon public debt up 36 pct Jan-Nov - Banks Assn.</title>
<headline>Lebanon public debt up 36 pct Jan-Nov - Banks Assn.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's public debt rose by more than 36 percent in the first 11 months of 1995, according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association on Saturday.</p>
<p>The cumulative deficit of income to expenditure was steady at 54 percent, the same figure as at the end of October, the association said. This compared with a target deficit for the year of 37.6 percent according to the budget law approved by parliament last January.</p>
<p>The association issued the following details of Lebanon's public finances (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>			    Dec 95  Sep 96  Oct 96  Nov 96 Dec95-Oct96</p>
<p>									   %</p>
<p>Revenues (Cumulative) 3,033    2,461    2,748    3,041</p>
<p>Monthly change			292	287	293</p>
<p> Expenses (Cumulative) 5,739  4,937    5,998    6,550</p>
<p> Monthly change		     778    1,061	552</p>
<p> Deficit (Cumulative)  2,706  2,476    3,250    3,509</p>
<p> Monthly change		     486	774     259</p>
<p> Ratio deficit to expenses	0.47     0.50     0.54   0.54</p>
<p> Monthly change		     0.02     0.04    (0.01)</p>
<p> Total debt	     14,09   17,787   18,279   19,172   36.17</p>
<p> Month change(%)		     5.87     2.77    4.88</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057</p>
